This README file contains information on the contents of the meta-de1soc-net layer.

Please see the corresponding sections below for details.

Purpose
=======

Gives the board a fixed, known address — 192.168.100.50 on end0 — via
systemd-networkd, instead of DHCP. This makes every SSH/scp step in the
build, deploy, and debug workflows deterministic (the guides hardcode
root@192.168.100.50) and lets the board talk directly to the flashing
machine (192.168.100.252) on the same wired segment without any DHCP
server present.

Contents
========

  conf/layer.conf
  recipes-net/de1soc-static-ip/de1soc-static-ip.bb
  recipes-net/de1soc-static-ip/files/
      20-wired-static.network    systemd-networkd config:
                                   Name=end0
                                   Address=192.168.100.50/24
                                   Gateway=192.168.100.1
                                   DNS=192.168.100.1

How it works
============

The recipe installs the .network file into /etc/systemd/network/.
systemd-networkd matches the end0 interface (the HPS EMAC) and applies the
static configuration at boot.

Verify on the board (UART console if SSH is unreachable):

  networkctl status end0    # expect 192.168.100.50, state routable

Changing the address
====================

1. Edit files/20-wired-static.network (keep the host side of the link in
   the same /24 — the flashing machine sits at 192.168.100.252)
2. Rebuild:  bitbake de1soc-static-ip -c cleansstate && bitbake de1soc-static-ip
             bitbake core-image-minimal
3. Update any guide/scripts that reference the old address.

Dependencies
============

  URI: https://github.com/altera-fpga/gsrd-socfpga.git
  branch: scarthgap

  Runtime: systemd-networkd (part of the GSRD core-image-minimal rootfs)

Adding the meta-de1soc-net layer to your build
==============================================

Run 'bitbake-layers add-layer meta-de1soc-net'

Then install the recipe in conf/local.conf:

  IMAGE_INSTALL:append = " de1soc-static-ip"

Patches
=======

This is a project-internal layer for the DE1-SoC FPGA Music Player
(TEC Computer Engineering). It is not submitted upstream.
